10. Voice and video calls — no bundled call SDK
   Calls use the browser's own WebRTC implementation (RTCPeerConnection / getUserMedia, part of every modern browser
   and of the Android System WebView); the call code in lib/calls/* and components/chat/call/* is PawNail's own.
   Network helpers, not bundled: Google's public STUN servers (stun.l.google.com), and — only when the operator
   configures it — Cloudflare Realtime TURN (https://developers.cloudflare.com/realtime/turn/) or the operator's own
   TURN server, which relay encrypted media they cannot decode. Signaling goes through Pusher Channels (pusher-js, MIT).
   The ZEGOCLOUD UIKit SDK previously used for calls has been removed (11/2026).
